<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yankton Sioux</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ihanktonwan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yankton, or Ihanktonwan, are one of the seven divisions of the Oceti Sakowin, speaking the Dakota language and long grouped with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yanktonai">Yanktonai</a> as the middle Sioux. In the 18th century they lived along the Missouri River in present-day South Dakota and Iowa, hunting bison and trading. By a treaty of 1858 they ceded most of their land to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and settled on the Yankton Reservation in South Dakota.</p></div>
